  "verdict_rationale": "Core contract mechanics pass: the driver locates the window from the recorded trace, renders the exact onset/end frames (steps 0 and 476, t 0.0 and 9.52) which match the window, prints onset/end steps and times, and demonstrably never reads the success predicate. Two gaps keep it short of an unqualified accept: (1) the contract requires reporting the visual finding, but debug_visual.py hardcodes visual_finding=None and never populates it; (2) with obj_z resting below the 0.85 threshold, the onset degenerates to step 0, so the window marks the recovery boundary rather than a mid-episode failure onset. The capability is usable for locate+render under those restrictions, so restrict rather than reject.",
